From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:07:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: rgb: use the connector type of the panel

The parallel RGB output always registers its panel bridge as LVDS, so
parallel RGB panels show up as LVDS connectors. Use the connector type
the panel reports, and keep LVDS for panels that do not report one.

Signed-off-by: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_rgb.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_rgb.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_rgb.c
index add3123e5..abef4b218 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_rgb.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_rgb.c
@@ -138,6 +138,7 @@ struct rockchip_rgb *rockchip_rgb_init(struct device *dev,
 
 	if (panel) {
 		bridge = drm_panel_bridge_add_typed(panel,
+						    panel->connector_type ?:
 						    DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_LVDS);
 		if (IS_ERR(bridge))
 			return ERR_CAST(bridge);
